.TH POKENUX 1 "2026-10-08" "Pokénux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pokenux \- explore Pokémon, play quizzes and collect virtual cards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pokenux
.RI [ --help | --version | --check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pokénux is a keyboard and mouse driven terminal application with a Pokédex,
quizzes and a virtual trading card collection. An Internet connection is needed
to fetch Pokémon and card data. The collection uses virtual currency only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command line usage.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.B --check
Check the installation and packaged resources without opening the interface
or making network requests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pokenux/
User settings, downloaded data, caches and the virtual collection database.
An absolute XDG_DATA_HOME overrides the parent data directory.
.PP
Package upgrades and removal do not delete these files.
.SH NOTES
The standalone Linux packages include a private Python runtime in
.IR /opt/pokenux .
They do not require or modify the system Python installation.
Pokénux is an independent fan project, unaffiliated with Pokémon's rights holders.
.SH BUGS
Report reproducible issues at
.UR https://github.com/FrancoisBasset/pokenux/issues
the project issue tracker
.UE .
